	"identifying_description": "(a) high necked pigeon-breast bodice of black silk net embroidered with black sequins and rhinestones over white silk satin: gathered into a shirred grosgrain cummerbund at waist; puffed 3/4 sleeve of silk net gathered at elbow; finished with ruffle cuff; square yoke at neck of white silk satin trimmed with black sequins embroidery; standing collar of the same; yoke and center front bodice trimmed with pink silk satin ribbon, pale velvet trim, and pink tassels; (b) full trained skirt of black silk net and silk lace embroidered with black sequins: black velvet bottom hem; knife-pleated cream chiffon around bottom; train and lower park of skirt lined with cream silk satin.\r\n\r\nLabel: \"Blancquaert, Court Dressmaker & Ladies Tailor, London",
	"web_text": "Blancquaert (England, active 1903–1941) Evening ensemble: bodice and skirt, ca. 1905Bodice: silk satin weave with overlay of silk net with gelatin sequins and overlay of handmade silk lace with metal (silver alloy) sequins and glass beads; silk chiffon with painted stripes; glass beads, gelatin sequins, glass rhinestones, and metal-wrapped silk thread; silk net with silk rosettes; glass beads, metal sequins, and purl; silk satin weave; machine made lace and net; silk satin tie with silk tassels; and silk velvet ribbon trim; Skirt: silk satin weave with overlay of silk net with gelatin sequins and overlay of handmade silk lace with metal (silver alloy) sequins and glass beads; and silk velvet ribbon trim Gift of Mrs. H. J. Brunnier, 61.12a–b Worn by Ann Weideman Brunnier (American, 1885–1970)",
